<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌡️ LIVE AIR TEMPERATURE</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/air_temperature_na/legend.png?v=na-tmp-20261014-0200-gdps-GDPS_15km_AirTemp_2m-n-5273396-hrrr-hrrr-hrrr.20261014-01-n-701862-rrfs_rrfs-ak-rrfs.20261014-00-n-678937-rrfs_rrfs-conus-rrfs.20261014-00-n-576889-rrfs_rrfs-na-rrfs.20261014-00-n-573803" width="600" alt="legend"><br>2 m air temperature (degF), FIXED key (-60..150 F) with a STEADY gradient on the map: the raster blends smoothly through blue-white extreme cold &rarr; gray-blue subfreezing &rarr; <b>royal-blue freezing wall (30-40)</b> &rarr; frigid turquoise/blues (40-55) &rarr; transitional lime/teals (55-70) &rarr; mellow yellows (70-85) &rarr; warming orange/golds (85-100) &rarr; <b>scorching pink/reds (100+) to HIGHEST+ 150</b>, passing exactly through every key color (key bars show the <b>LOWEST -60</b> to <b>HIGHEST+ 150</b> band centers). Same temperature always shows the same color; every color is brightened so nothing renders dark. Freezing (32 F) sits inside the royal-blue wall.</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis, HRRR + RRFS-NA, GDPS fallback)</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3km 2m analysis (CONUS domain) + NOAA RRFS North American output (broad domain) + ECCC GDPS 15km fallback<br/><a href="https://gsl.noaa.gov/rrfs/">https://gsl.noaa.gov/rrfs/</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p><p><b>Coverage Selector</b> — one coverage at a time (Pro switches exclusively; Web/app: uncheck the others):<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Air_Temperature_Basin.kml">Great Lakes Basin Coverage</a><br>◉ <b>North America Coverage</b> (this view)<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Air_Temperature_Extended.kml">Extended North America Coverage</a><br>Add once: <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Air_Temperature_Coverage.kml">Coverage collection file</a> (all three as toggles).</p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE AIR TEMPERATURE</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p>2 m air temperature (degF), FIXED key (-60..150 F) with a STEADY gradient on the map: the raster blends smoothly through blue-white extreme cold &rarr; gray-blue subfreezing &rarr; <b>royal-blue freezing wall (30-40)</b> &rarr; frigid turquoise/blues (40-55) &rarr; transitional lime/teals (55-70) &rarr; mellow yellows (70-85) &rarr; warming orange/golds (85-100) &rarr; <b>scorching pink/reds (100+) to HIGHEST+ 150</b>, passing exactly through every key color (key bars show the <b>LOWEST -60</b> to <b>HIGHEST+ 150</b> band centers). Same temperature always shows the same color; every color is brightened so nothing renders dark. Freezing (32 F) sits inside the royal-blue wall.</p><p><b>Coverage:</b> North America Coverage<br><b>Precedence:</b> HRRR valid > RRFS-NA valid > GDPS valid > transparent. Explicit per-pixel validity masks; never blended, never duplicated.<br><b>Provenance:</b> {'hrrr': 'hrrr hrrr.20261014/01 n=701862', 'rrfs_rrfs-na rrfs.20261014/00': 'n=573803', 'rrfs_rrfs-conus rrfs.20261014/00': 'n=576889', 'rrfs_rrfs-ak rrfs.20261014/00': 'n=678937', 'gdps': 'GDPS_15km_AirTemp_2m n=5273396'}</p><p><b>Coverage Selector</b> — one coverage at a time (Pro switches exclusively; Web/app: uncheck the others):<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Air_Temperature_Basin.kml">Great Lakes Basin Coverage</a><br>◉ <b>North America Coverage</b> (this view)<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Air_Temperature_Extended.kml">Extended North America Coverage</a><br>Add once: <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Air_Temperature_Coverage.kml">Coverage collection file</a> (all three as toggles).</p>]]></description>
